<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-WMC sells Thevenard petroleum assets.</title>
<headline>RTRS-WMC sells Thevenard petroleum assets.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>WMC Ltd said on Tuesday it had sold its Thevenard petroleum assets to Shell Australia Development Ltd, a unit of the Royal Dutch/Shell group.</p>
<p>WAPET is two sevenths owned each by Chevron, Shell, Texaco Inc, and one seventh by new Mobil unit Ampolex Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale is expected to be completed by year end and is subject to government approvals,&quot; WMC said.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale was initiated prior to our announcement in August 1996 to sell the group's petroleum businesses in Australia, USA and New Zealand, which is still expected to be completed by the end of this financial year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>WMC did not say how much it had received for the assets, which are operated by WAPET (West Australian Petroleum Pty Ltd), and include interests in 17 permits.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
